-----------------------------------------------Linux Package Managers and Commands---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. What is a Package Manager?
A package manager is a tool used to install, update, remove, and manage software packages on Linux.

It automatically handles:

Installing software
Removing software
Updating software
Installing dependencies
Searching for packages
Checking installed packages
Package Manager
      |
      +-- Install
      +-- Update
      +-- Remove
      +-- Search
      +-- Upgrade
      +-- Dependencies

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. APT - Debian / Ubuntu / Parrot / Kali

APT is commonly used on Debian-based distributions.

sudo apt update

Updates the local package information.

sudo apt upgrade

Upgrades installed packages.

Install a package
sudo apt install package_name

Example:

sudo apt install nmap
Remove a package
sudo apt remove package_name

Example:

sudo apt remove nmap
Remove package and configuration files

Search for a package
apt search package_name

Example:

apt search wireshark
Show package information
apt show package_name

Example:

apt show nmap
List installed packages
apt list --installed

Check for upgradable packages
apt list --upgradable

Remove unused dependencies
sudo apt autoremove
Clean downloaded package files

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. DPKG - Debian Package Manager

dpkg works directly with .deb packages.

Install a .deb package
sudo dpkg -i package.deb

Remove a package
sudo dpkg -r package_name

List installed packages
dpkg -l

Check whether a package is installed
dpkg -l | grep package_name

Show package information
dpkg -s package_name

List files installed by a package
dpkg -L package_name

Example:

dpkg -L nmap

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5. YUM - Red Hat-Based Systems

yum was traditionally used by RHEL/CentOS and related distributions.

Install
sudo yum install package_name

Update
sudo yum update

Remove
sudo yum remove package_name

Search
yum search package_name

List installed packages
yum list installed

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6. DNF - Modern Red Hat Package Manager

dnf is the modern package manager used by distributions such as Fedora and newer RHEL-based systems.

Install
sudo dnf install package_name

Update
sudo dnf update

Remove
sudo dnf remove package_name

Search
dnf search package_name

Show package information
dnf info package_name

List installed packages
dnf list installed

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7. Pacman - Arch Linux

pacman is the package manager used by Arch Linux and Arch-based distributions.

Update package database and upgrade system
sudo pacman -Syu

Install
sudo pacman -S package_name

Example:
sudo pacman -S nmap

Remove
sudo pacman -R package_name

Search
pacman -Ss package_name

Search installed packages
pacman -Qs package_name

List installed packages
pacman -Q

Show package information
pacman -Si package_name
sudo apt clean

